com/users/ZycroNeXuS/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZycroNeXuS/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZycroNeXuS/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ZycroNeXuS/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-21T03:02:16Z","updated_at":"2025-01-21T03:02:16Z","body":"I believe I've narrowed down that this happens as a result of some bug that occasionally occurs when saving with Ctrl+S with the Godot Dialogue Manager extension, which I can see that @Athsmar has, and its happened to me too. [There's an issue on that extension's Github](https://github.com/nathanhoad/godot_dialogue_manager/issues/723), though I've been finding this bug difficult to reproduce and document so if you can reproduce it yourself with some logs or videos or something I'm sure that would be helpful in getting this fixed.\n\nFor anybody who stumbles across this first, you can kind of get around this bug with some mindfulness, make sure to go back to your main scene and save again before you close the editor, and that should eliminate the issue until it's fixed. It also doesn't seem to happen if you save dialogues with the save button (in my experience). If it's too late, and you've already closed with the broken scene, I'm afraid you either have to load from backup or rebuild it (which might not be as bad as you think, depending on the size of your project and how much functionality you have saved in other scenes, only took me a couple hours).","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2603527113/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2815642156","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99863#issuecomment-281